most. OBJECTIVE To evaluate whether delivering more intensive insulin-adherence interventions only to individuals with 
type 2 diabetes predicted to benefit most was more effective than delivering a lower-intensity intervention to a larger 
group of unselected individuals. DESIGN, SETTING, AND PARTICIPANTS This 3-arm pragmatic randomized clinical trial used 
data from Horizon, the largest health insurer in New Jersey, on 6000 participants 18 years or older with type 2 diabetes
who were receiving basal insulin. Patients were excluded if they were insured by Medicaid or Medicare or had fewer than 
3 months of continuous enrollment. The study was conducted from July 7, 2016, through October 5, 2017. Analyses were 
